Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 44-45 Feralas]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Back to Kalimdor: Ratchet - Theramore, Guard Jameson's sword and Tabetha's farm in Dustwallow Marsh, then Feralas again by flight: Kindal's sprite darters and the Grimtotem camp, the Writhing Deep for the lost courier, a Hippogryph Egg for the Egg-O-Matic, the Feathermoon hand-ins, and Rockbiter and Wandering Shay in the north-west. Ends at Feathermoon's flight master for Zul'Farrak.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  this chapter wants level 46. Its quests need 36-44 (Rockbiter's two need 44), but its mobs climb from the Dustwallow oozes (38-40) and the Grimtotem camp (41-44) to the Woodpaw gnolls (42-44), the Zukk'ash hive (44-46) and the Frayfeather nests (44-47); the north-west round Rockbiter and Shay is 47-52 with elite giants beside Rockbiter, which is why it is last. You arrive at about 44. Under 45 when Feathermoon is done: skip the giants leg (its first line says so) and go straight to Fyldren Moonfeather
[OC]|cffffffffFeralas II|r  -  you start on the Ratchet dock off the Booty Bay boat, hearth = Booty Bay; it moves to Feathermoon in this chapter. About 31,000 quest XP from 9 hand-ins and 55s of quest money; every quest is plain except the "only if" lines. Camp Mojache (75,44) is still a Horde town with level-55 guards: every Feralas leg goes round it to the south
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r givers, hand-ins, objects and mob positions come from the DB; the Dustwallow and Feralas roads, the Feathermoon ferry and its docks are not in it (unverified)
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Tabetha's Task (2861, Bink, chapter 49) is handed in at Tabetha. The Super Egg-O-Matic (2741, chapter 46) gets its Hippogryph Egg here; the hand-in is the Egg-O-Matic in Gadgetzan, chapter 53. If you took them in chapter 49, Alliance Trauma (6625) and I Got Nothin' Left! (6609) are handed in on the Theramore leg. Riding through untouched: Nekrum's Medallion (2991), The Witch Doctor's Head (96770), Screecher Spirits (3520, complete) and Scarab Shells (2865) for Zul'Farrak in chapter 51; Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar (1475) and Cortello's Riddle (624) for the next round
[OC]|cffffcc00Training:|r no shaman trainer in Dustwallow or Feralas; the next row waits for Ironforge

[OC]|cffffffffRatchet and Theramore|r  -  flight to Theramore, then the town quests
At [TAR16227 Bragok], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Theramore]|r [G63.1,37.2 The Barrens]
At [TAR271167 Guard Jameson], [QA98233 Sword in the Slime] (3,450 XP + 55s at the hand-in: Jameson's Training Sword from the Corrosive Swamp Oozes beside Tabetha's farm) [G65.5,45.4 Dustwallow Marsh]
[O]Only if you hold Alliance Trauma and have First Aid 225: at [TAR12939 Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen], [QT6625] (970 XP) [QA6624 Triage] (3,900 XP: save 15 patients with Triage Bandages before 6 of them die) [G67.8,49.0 Dustwallow Marsh]
[O]Only with Triage: tend the patients with the Triage Bandages, Critically Injured first, then Badly Injured, then Injured (that they lie in Gustaf's building is Classic knowledge, unverified) [QC6624] [G67.8,49.0 Dustwallow Marsh]
[O]Only with Triage done: at [TAR12939 Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen], [QT6624] (3,900 XP) [G67.8,49.0 Dustwallow Marsh]

[OC]|cffffffffTabetha's farm|r  -  west out of Theramore by road, about 23 units (the road is not in the data, unverified; its mobs are 35-41)
Ride west out of Theramore to Tabetha's farm (road unverified) [G46.1,57.1 Dustwallow Marsh]
At [TAR6546 Tabetha], [QT2861] (405 XP) [G46.1,57.1 Dustwallow Marsh]
At [TAR6546 Tabetha], [QA2846 Tiara of the Deep] (6,050 XP + 65s at the hand-in: Hydromancer Velratha's tiara in Zul'Farrak, chapter 51; Tabetha takes it in chapter 52) [G46.1,57.1 Dustwallow Marsh]
[OC]|cFFFF0000Danger:|r Elder Daggermaws (level 48-49, four or five over you) lie east of the farm, the nearest about one unit away at 46.8,57.7: keep to the west side. Their reaction is not in the data (unverified)
Kill [TAR4392 Corrosive Swamp Ooze] (38-40) for Jameson's Training Sword [QC98233] (~33% - budget ~3 kills). Three stand just west of the farm; the other seven are east among the elite Bubbling Swamp Oozes (39-40): finish on the west three if you can [G45.2,58.4 Dustwallow Marsh]
[O]Only if you hold I Got Nothin' Left! and have Fishing 225: at [TAR12919 Nat Pagle] on his island south of Theramore (swim out from the south shore, unverified), [QT6609] (970 XP) [QA6607 Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme] (3,900 XP at the hand-in: Feralas Ahi on this chapter's route, the other three fish in the Swamp of Sorrows, Desolace and Stranglethorn; hand-in on a later Theramore pass) [G58.6,60.1 Dustwallow Marsh]
At [TAR271167 Guard Jameson] back in Theramore, [QT98233] (3,450 XP + 55s) [G65.5,45.4 Dustwallow Marsh]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (98233):|r Jameson's Backup Sword is a two-hand sword: a shaman cannot use it, vendor it (1g 65s 58c)
At [TAR4321 Baldruc], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Thalanaar]|r [G67.5,51.3 Dustwallow Marsh]

[OC]|cffffffffKindal Moonweaver and the Grimtotem camp|r  -  west from Thalanaar round the south side of Camp Mojache, about 24 units. Grimtotem Naturalists 41-42, Raiders 42-43, Shamans 43-44; Sprite Darters (43-45) wander the camp
[OC]|cFFFF0000Danger:|r the Gordok ogres of Dire Maul (Enforcers 53-54, Ogre-Mages 52-53, elite) stand about two units west of Kindal: do not step west of her. Namida Grimtotem (43, elite) stands at the camp's north end (67.5,39.0): leave her
At [TAR7956 Kindal Moonweaver], [QA2969 Freedom for All Creatures] (3,150 XP: free at least 6 Sprite Darters from the Grimtotem pen with the Bamboo Cage Key; Kindal must survive; 6 minutes) [G65.9,45.6 Feralas]
|cFFFF0000ESCORT|r Clear the Grimtotems round the pen first, then open it with the Bamboo Cage Key and keep Kindal and at least 6 Sprite Darters alive until she leaves. These kills do not count for Doling Justice (it opens only after this hand-in): keep the pull small. How the event runs is Classic knowledge, unverified [QC2969] [G66.5,46.9 Feralas]
At [TAR7956 Kindal Moonweaver], [QT2969] (3,150 XP) [G65.9,45.6 Feralas]
At [TAR7957 Jer'kai Moonweaver] beside her, [QA2970 Doling Justice] (3,150 XP: 12 Grimtotem Naturalists, 10 Grimtotem Raiders and 6 Grimtotem Shamans) [G66.0,45.6 Feralas]
Kill 12 [TAR7726 Grimtotem Naturalist], 10 [TAR7725 Grimtotem Raider] and 6 [TAR7727 Grimtotem Shaman] in the Grimtotem camp (x66-70 y38-48) [QC2970] [G67.9,43.5 Feralas]
[O]Only if a Diseased Nature Staff drops or turns up: right-click it to start [QA95555 Corrupted Nature] (4,700 XP + 75s: find the source of the staff's corruption in Feralas). The staff's source and the quest's hand-in are not in the data; the two Dead Diseased Grimtotem Shaman corpses here are the likeliest place by their name only (unverified) [G69.5,43.2 Feralas]
At [TAR7957 Jer'kai Moonweaver], [QT2970] (3,150 XP) [QA2972 Doling Justice] (5,250 XP at the hand-in: Jer'kai's Signet Ring to Tyrande Whisperwind in Darnassus, chapter 55) [G66.0,45.6 Feralas]

[OC]|cffffffffThe Woodpaw camps and the Writhing Deep|r  -  south-east to the Woodpaw camps (Mystics and Reavers 42-43, Alphas 43-44), then south into the Zukk'ash hive (44-46)
[O]Only with Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme in your log: fish a Feralas Ahi in the Verdantis River on the way [CI16967,1] [G62.8,51.5 Feralas]
At the Large Leather Backpacks in the Woodpaw camp, [QA4135 The Writhing Deep] (3,050 XP: find Raschal in the Writhing Deep, south of the camps). Woodpaw Alphas, Mystics and Reavers stand on the backpacks [G73.3,56.3 Feralas]
[OC]|cFFFF0000Danger:|r the pod sits among Zukk'ash Tunnelers (45-46), Wasps (44-45) and Stingers (45-46), with Fel Interlopers (45-48; reaction not in the data, unverified) a few steps off: one or two levels over you. The Tyrant of the Hive (46) is east at 77.7,62.3 and the rare Qirot (47) nearby: come at the pod from the west and stay on its west side
At the Zukk'ash Pod in the Writhing Deep, [QT4135] (3,050 XP) [QA4265 Freed from the Hive] (4,050 XP at Ginro Hearthkindle in Feathermoon) [G72.1,63.7 Feralas]
Free Raschal at the Zukk'ash Pod (use the pod again; Classic knowledge, unverified) [QC4265] [G72.1,63.7 Feralas]

[OC]|cffffffffThe Frayfeather nests|r  -  west-south-west from the hive, about 20 units, for the Egg-O-Matic's egg. The eggs (nine in the DB at x54-59 y74-78) lie among Frayfeather Stagwings (44-45), Skystormers (45-46) and Patriarchs (46-47), a Cursed Sycamore (45) and the rare Antilus the Soarer (48); the Gordunni Battlemasters and Mage-Lords (45-46) of the ogre camp stand two or three units north. None of them is elite in the data, but most are one to three levels over you: pull one at a time and take the first egg you can reach
Loot a Hippogryph Egg from a nest for The Super Egg-O-Matic [CI8564,1] [G58.0,76.3 Feralas]
[OC]|cffffcc00OOX-22/FE:|r if the OOX-22/FE Distress Beacon drops in this chapter (0.34% per kill), it starts the same pair as in chapter 47: the homing robot is in the cave near Feral Scar Vale (53.4,55.7, on the ride to the dock) and its escort ends at the Forgotten Coast dock; Rescue OOX-22/FE! is then handed in at Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay in the next round, as no Booty Bay visit is left in this one

[OC]|cffffffffFeathermoon Stronghold|r  -  north-west to the Forgotten Coast dock and the boat to Sardor Isle. Vale Screamers (level 60) are in the DB across central Feralas, the dock included; whether they are live and hostile is unverified. Sea Elementals (48-49) and elite striders work the shore: go straight to the dock
Ride north-west to the Forgotten Coast dock and take the boat to Feathermoon Stronghold (the ferry and its island dock are not in the data, unverified) [G45.6,43.4 Feralas]
At [TAR7736 Innkeeper Shyria], bind your Hearthstone to [S Feathermoon] (the Booty Bay bind from chapter 49 ends here) [G31.0,43.5 Feralas]
At [TAR7880 Ginro Hearthkindle], [QT4265] (4,050 XP) [QA4266 A Hero's Welcome] (6,050 XP: speak with Shandris Feathermoon) [G31.9,45.1 Feralas]
At [TAR3936 Shandris Feathermoon], [QT4266] (6,050 XP) [QA4267 Rise of the Silithid] (405 XP at the hand-in: Raschal's Report to Gracina Spiritmight in Darnassus, chapter 55) [G30.3,46.2 Feralas]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (4266):|r take the Sanctimonial Rod (2H staff, 26.45 dps, +4 Sta +17 Spi, +38 spell damage, 488.8) over the Ceremonial Elven Blade (one-hand dagger, 380.1); neither beats Rage of the Storm or Bonebiter: vendor it (2g 13s 77c)
At [TAR7764 Troyas Moonbreeze], [QA2939 In Search of Knowledge] (420 XP at the hand-in: talk to Daryn Lightwind in Rut'theran Village, chapter 55) [G31.8,45.5 Feralas]

[OC]|cffffffffRockbiter and Wandering Shay|r  -  this leg's mobs are 47-52 and elite giants stand beside Rockbiter. If you are under 45, skip the leg: there is no later Feralas visit in this round, so the two quests are then lost to it (do not accept them in that case) and you go straight to the last lines at Fyldren Moonfeather
[OC]|cFFFF0000Danger:|r every mob in the north-west is three to eight levels over you: Ironfur Patriarchs (48-49) and Groddoc Thunderers (49-50) on the way north; round Rockbiter Enraged Mountain Giants (49-50), Rampaging Chimaeras, Lost Daughters and Vengeful Sons (51) and The Giant (52), with the elite Cliff Giants (49-50) and Land Walkers (48-49) about 1.5 units west of him; round Shay the Northspring and Dreamspring harpies (48-51) and the elite Edana Hatetalon (50) three units off. Ride, do not pull; if you die, run back from the spirit healer. Whether the Forever-new mobs here are hostile is unverified
Take the boat back to the Forgotten Coast dock (ferry unverified) and ride north, about 21 units [G45.6,43.4 Feralas]
At [TAR7765 Rockbiter], [QA2844 The Giant Guardian] (3,400 XP: find the lost night elf girl to the north) [G42.4,22.0 Feralas]
At [TAR7774 Shay Leafrunner], about 12 units north-west, [QT2844] (3,400 XP) [QA2845 Wandering Shay] (4,550 XP: her bell from the chest, then take her to Rockbiter's camp) [G38.2,10.3 Feralas]
Open Shay's Chest beside her for Shay's Bell [CI9189,1] [G38.2,10.3 Feralas]
|cFFFF0000ESCORT|r Take Shay Leafrunner back south-east to Rockbiter's camp, about 12 units through the harpies and giants; if she wanders off, ring the bell to call her back (Classic knowledge, unverified) [QC2845] [G42.4,22.0 Feralas]
At [TAR7765 Rockbiter], [QT2845] (4,550 XP) [G42.4,22.0 Feralas]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (2845):|r take the Vinehedge Cinch (leather waist, +14 Str +3 Sta, 28.0); Granite Grips are plate. Wear it over the Violet Sash or Grappler's Belt; keep the Deathmage Sash (39.4) if you wear it; against the Twilight Initiate's Belt (29.8 central, 22.8 conservative) it is level: keep the Belt. Otherwise vendor it (53s 33c)
|cFFfff8a3Hearth to [H Feathermoon]|r (on cooldown: ride south to the dock and take the boat) [G42.4,22.0 Feralas]

[OC]|cffffffffFeathermoon: the end|r  -  chapter 51 flies from Fyldren Moonfeather
[O]If you took Corrupted Nature and no one has taken it: abandon it [QS95555] [G30.2,43.2 Feralas]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r handed in here: Sword in the Slime (98233), Tabetha's Task (2861), Freedom for All Creatures (2969), Doling Justice (2970), The Writhing Deep (4135), Freed from the Hive (4265), A Hero's Welcome (4266), The Giant Guardian (2844) and Wandering Shay (2845) unless you skipped the giants leg; if you had them, Alliance Trauma (6625), Triage (6624) and I Got Nothin' Left! (6609). In the log for later: Tiara of the Deep (2846, the tiara in Zul'Farrak, chapter 51; Tabetha in chapter 52); Doling Justice (2972), Rise of the Silithid (4267) and In Search of Knowledge (2939) for Darnassus and Rut'theran, chapter 55; The Super Egg-O-Matic (2741, with the egg, Gadgetzan in chapter 53); Nekrum's Medallion (2991), The Witch Doctor's Head (96770), Screecher Spirits (3520, complete) and Scarab Shells (2865) for Zul'Farrak, chapter 51; Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar (1475) and Cortello's Riddle (624) for the next round; if taken, Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme (6607, a later Theramore pass) and Find / Rescue OOX-22/FE! (2766 / 2767, next round). Hearth = Feathermoon. Quest money this chapter: 55s
Walk to the hippogryph master [TAR8019 Fyldren Moonfeather]; chapter 51 starts here with the flight to Gadgetzan [G30.2,43.2 Feralas]

